    {
      "url": "https://registrar.ucsf.edu/diplomas/how-obtain-your-diploma",
      "path": "/diplomas/how-obtain-your-diploma",
      "slug": "diplomas-how-obtain-your-diploma",
      "title": "How To Obtain Your Diploma",
      "pageTitle": "Office of the Registrar",
      "summary": "How To Obtain Your Diploma Diplomas and certificates are available eight to twelve weeks after the end of the academic term in which you graduated. You will be notified when diplomas are available",
      "bodyHtml": "<main> <div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div data-drupal-messages-fallback></div> </div> </div> <a tabindex=\"-1\"></a> <div> <div> <div> <article> <div> <div><h1>How To Obtain Your Diploma</h1><p>Diplomas and certificates are available eight to twelve weeks after the end of the academic term in which you graduated. You will be notified when diplomas are available. You can pick up your diploma or certificate in person, or we can mail it to you.&nbsp;The university cannot guarantee availability of diplomas or certificates that have not been claimed within three&nbsp;years.</p><p>If we mail your diploma or certificate and it is returned as undeliverable, the fee to mail it again will be $25. Our office will replace diplomas and certificates free of charge only if you contact us within two weeks of receipt for damage or six months of shipment for non-delivery. Beyond these time periods, our standard fees for <a href=\"/diploma-or-certificate-reissue\">diploma reissue</a> and mailing will apply.</p><h2>In Person</h2><p>Please bring a picture ID to MU-200W on the Parnassus campus (on the 2nd floor of Millberry Union, next to the library). Our hours are&nbsp;Monday–Friday, 8 a.m. – 1:30 p.m. &amp; 3 p.m. – 5 p.m.</p><h2>3rd Party Pickup</h2><p>To authorize release of your diploma or certificate to a third party please complete the steps detailed on <a href=\"https://ucsf.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_80QAfEWLpdZw8yG\" target=\"_blank\">this form</a>.</p><p>The university cannot guarantee availability of diplomas or certificates that have not been claimed within three years. For these documents, please <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#\">contact the Office of the Registrar</a> first to confirm availability.</p><h2>Mail</h2><p>The mailing fee is $20; however, we will mail diplomas or certificates at no charge for School of Nursing students (MEPN, DNP, Supplemental Studies in Advanced Practice in Nursing, Nursing MS, Nursing PhD, and Sociology PhD) who graduated in spring 2006 or later, Master of Translational Medicine students who graduated in spring 2020 or later, School of Pharmacy students who graduated between fall 2006 and fall 2012, and Equity in Brain Health students.</p><p><strong>We ship diplomas destined to U.S. addresses by U.S. Postal Service First-Class Mail. A signature will be required upon delivery.</strong></p><p>If we mail your diploma and it is returned as undeliverable, the fee to mail it again will be $25.</p><details contenteditable=\"false\"><summary>Winter 2026 and Prior Graduates</summary><article><p>Please <a href=\"https://tiny.ucsf.edu/DiplomaMailing\" target=\"_blank\">order your diploma mailing online</a>.</p><p>The university cannot guarantee availability of diplomas or certificates that have not been claimed within three years. For these documents, please <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#\">contact the Office of the Registrar</a> first to confirm availability.</p></article></details><details contenteditable=\"false\"><summary>Spring 2026 and Future Graduates</summary><article><p>Our office will contact you after your diplomas/certificates are ready for pickup or mailing. In the meantime, please ensure that your mailing address, phone number, and personal email in the Profile section of your <a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/studentportal/\" target=\"_blank\">Student Portal</a> are up to date. Please read about <a href=\"/student-records/alumni-portal-access\">Student Portal Access for Alumni and Former Students</a>.</p></article></details><p>&nbsp;</p><details contenteditable=\"false\"><summary>Placing your order via Check, Cashier's Check, or Money Order?</summary><article><p><strong>Please include the following information:</strong></p><ul><li>Your name when you graduated from UCSF and, if different, your current name</li><li>Program or school attended</li><li>Degree</li><li>Date of graduation</li><li>Address to send diploma or certificate (a signature is required upon delivery)</li><li>Your signature</li></ul><p>Please sign your request and enclose a check, money order, or cashier's check payable to UC Regents for the total fee or provide your Visa, MasterCard, Discover, or American Express information, including&nbsp;your card number, the expiration date, and the three-digit code from the signature block on the back of the card. For credit card orders only, you may fax your request to (415)&nbsp;476-9690. We cannot accept credit card information by e-mail.</p><p><strong>Mail your request to:</strong><br>Transcript &amp; Diploma Unit<br>UCSF Office of the Registrar<br>UCSF Box 0244<br>500 Parnassus Ave MU-200W<br>San Francisco CA 94143</p><p>Fax: (415)&nbsp;476-9690</p></article></details><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>If you have questions, please call (415) 476-4356.</strong></p></div> <section> </section> </div> </article> </div> </div>\n<div> <div> <div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <aside> <div> <nav role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"block-sb-nine-mainmenu-menu\"> <h2><span>Diplomas</span></h2> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/diploma-overview\">Diploma Overview</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/how-obtain-your-diploma\" aria-current=\"page\">How To Obtain Your Diploma</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/diploma-or-certificate-reissue\">Diploma or Certificate Reissue</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/diploma-certification-boards\">Diploma Certification for the Boards</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/diploma-mailing-request-form\">Diploma Mailing Request Form</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/diplomas/access-electronic-systems-after-graduation\">Access to Electronic Systems After Graduation</a> </li> </ul> </nav> </div> </aside> <aside> <div> <div> <div> <h2>Quick Links</h2> <div> <div><p><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/studentportal/\" target=\"_blank\">Student Portal Login</a><br><a href=\"/academic-calendar\">Academic Calendar</a><br><a href=\"http://catalog.ucsf.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">General Catalog</a><br><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/courseschedule/\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule of Classes</a><br><a href=\"/forms\">Forms</a><br><a href=\"/registration/deadlineshome\">Deadlines</a><br><a href=\"/registration/fees\">Fees</a><br><a href=\"/registration/residency\" title=\"California Residency\">California Residency</a></p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </aside> </div> </div> </div> </main>",
