    {
      "url": "https://registrar.ucsf.edu/student-records/alumni-portal-access",
      "path": "/student-records/alumni-portal-access",
      "slug": "student-records-alumni-portal-access",
      "title": "Office of the Registrar",
      "pageTitle": "Office of the Registrar",
      "summary": "Student Portal Access for Alumni & Former Students Alumni whose UCSF student record includes their Gmail account can use their Google credentials to log in to the student portal. If you do not have a Gmail account in your student record, or",
      "bodyHtml": "<main> <div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div data-drupal-messages-fallback></div> </div> </div> <a tabindex=\"-1\"></a> <div> <div> <div> <article> <div> <div><h2>Student Portal Access for Alumni &amp; Former Students</h2><p>Alumni whose UCSF student record includes their Gmail account can use their Google credentials to log in to the student portal.&nbsp;If you do not have a Gmail account in your student record, or if you need to update the telephone number that you encounter during the login process, please <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#c7b5a2a0aeb4b3b5a6b587b2a4b4a1e9a2a3b2f8b4b2a5ada2a4b3fa86abb2aaa9aee2f5f794b3b2a3a2a9b3e2f5f797a8b5b3a6abe2f5f786a4a4a2b4b4\">contact the Office of the Registrar</a>.</p><h2>Login Instructions</h2><p>Navigate to the <a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/studentportal/\">student portal login page</a>.</p><p>Click “Log in with Google ID”, which will take you to the “Sign in with Google” page.&nbsp;This Google page will ask you to enter the e-mail address or phone number associated with your Google account.</p>\n<div> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/tkssra11031/files/styles/large/public/img/googlesignin.png.webp?itok=sNJqV7Ht\" width=\"367\" height=\"365\" alt=\"Google Sign-In Page\"> </div> <p>After you enter your e-mail address or phone number on this Google sign-in page, you will be asked to enter the Google password associated with that e-mail address or phone number.</p>\n<div> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/tkssra11031/files/styles/large/public/img/googlepassword.png.webp?itok=u_c3rfRn\" width=\"281\" height=\"353\" alt=\"Google Password Page\"> </div> <p>The sign-in page will direct you to UCSF’s two-factor authentication system, OKTA. &nbsp;Select the form of verification that you wish OKTA to use.&nbsp;You can choose to receive a verification code by text or a telephone call; in each case, OKTA will use the telephone number in your UCSF student records.&nbsp;(Note: This telephone number may or may not be the telephone number that is associated with your Google account.)</p>\n<div> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/tkssra11031/files/styles/large/public/img/okta2factor.png.webp?itok=rVHoqXCL\" width=\"330\" height=\"340\" alt=\"Okta 2-Factor Authentication\"> </div> <p>After selecting your authentication method, enter the code in OKTA that you receive by text message or telephone call.</p><p>Alumni who do not have a Gmail account in their student record or who do not have access to the telephone number in their student record may contact the Office of the Registrar for assistance at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#fc8e999b958f888e9d8ebc899f8f9ad2999889\"><span>[email&#160;protected]</span></a> or 415-476-8280.</p><p>Current students should use MyAccess to access the student portal, not their Google credentials.</p>\n<div> <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/sites/g/files/tkssra11031/files/styles/large/public/img/oktaauthentication.png.webp?itok=vG6aZNkS\" width=\"344\" height=\"391\" alt=\"Okta Authentication\"> </div> </div> <section> </section> </div> </article> </div> </div>\n<div> <div> <div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <aside> <div> <nav role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"block-sb-nine-mainmenu-menu\"> <h2><span>Student Records</span></h2> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/name-change\">Legal Name Change</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/preferred\">Lived Names</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/substitution\">Petition for Substitution of Course</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/examination\">Credit by Examination</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/disclosure\">Disclosure of Information - FERPA</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/grades\">Grades</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/dns\">Nursing DNS to PhD Conversion</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/nondisc\">Nondiscrimination Policy Statement</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/student-records/alumni-portal-access\" aria-current=\"page\">Student Portal Access for Alumni &amp; Former Students</a> </li> </ul> </nav> </div> </aside> <aside> <div> <div> <div> <h2>Quick Links</h2> <div> <div><p><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/studentportal/\" target=\"_blank\">Student Portal Login</a><br><a href=\"/academic-calendar\">Academic Calendar</a><br><a href=\"http://catalog.ucsf.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">General Catalog</a><br><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/courseschedule/\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule of Classes</a><br><a href=\"/forms\">Forms</a><br><a href=\"/registration/deadlineshome\">Deadlines</a><br><a href=\"/registration/fees\">Fees</a><br><a href=\"/registration/residency\" title=\"California Residency\">California Residency</a></p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </aside> </div> </div> </div> </main>",
