      "url": "https://registrar.ucsf.edu/registration/fees/summer2025",
      "path": "/registration/fees/summer2025",
      "slug": "registration-fees-summer2025",
      "title": "Summer Session 2025",
      "pageTitle": "Office of the Registrar",
      "summary": "Summer Session 2025 Fees for summer 2025 appear below. The tuition, fees, and charges posted here are estimates based on currently approved amounts",
      "bodyHtml": "<main> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div>\n</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div> <div data-drupal-messages-fallback></div> </div> </div> <a tabindex=\"-1\"></a> <div> <div> <div> <article> <div> <div><h1>Summer Session 2025</h1><p>Fees for summer 2025 appear below.</p><p>The tuition, fees, and charges posted here are estimates based on currently approved amounts.&nbsp;<strong>These figures may not be final.</strong>&nbsp;Actual tuition, fees, and charges are subject to change by the Regents of the University of California and could be affected by state funding reductions. Accordingly, final approved levels (and thus a student's final balance due) may differ from the amounts shown.</p><p>Some or all instruction for all or part of the Academic Year may be delivered remotely.&nbsp; Tuition and fees have been set regardless of the method of instruction and will not be refunded in the event instruction occurs remotely for any part of the Academic Year.&nbsp; Figures for tuition and fees represent currently approved or proposed amounts and may not be final.&nbsp; Actual tuition and fees are subject to change by the University of California as determined to be necessary or appropriate.&nbsp; Final approved tuition and fee levels may differ from the amounts presented.</p><table><caption>Summer Session 1</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registration Fee</td><td>$2,230.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$2,230.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><p><strong>Total</strong></p><table><caption>Summer Session 2</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registration Fee</td><td>$2,230.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$2,230.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Summer Term</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registration Fee</td><td>$4,460.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$4,460.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Pharmacy 1 and 3</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer Student Services Fee</td><td>$80.00</td></tr><tr><td>Tuition</td><td>$4,380.00</td></tr><tr><td>Associated Students of School of Pharmacy</td><td>$15.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td>Professional Degree Supplemental Tuition</td><td>$8,540.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$15,261.00</td></tr></tbody></table><table><caption>Pharmacy 2</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer Student Services Fee</td><td>$80.00</td></tr><tr><td>Tuition</td><td>$4,380.00</td></tr><tr><td>Associated Students of School of Pharmacy</td><td>$15.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$1,723.00</td></tr><tr><td>Professional Degree Supplemental Tuition</td><td>$8,540.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$14,738.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Medicine, Dentistry, Nursing - MS (selected specialties)</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer Student Services Fee</td><td>$80.00</td></tr><tr><td>Tuition</td><td>$4,380.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$4,460.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Physical Therapy</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer Student Services Fee</td><td>$80.00</td></tr><tr><td>Tuition</td><td>$4,380.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$6,706.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Post Baccalaureate Program - Medicine</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,492.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$2,492.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Artificial Intelligence and Computational Drug Discovery and Development - MS&nbsp;</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$15,000.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$17,246.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>International Dentistry Program (IDP) - Level 2</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$17,929.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$3,277.00</td></tr><tr><td>Instruments, Equipment and Supplies</td><td>$4,988.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$26,194.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><table><caption>International Dentistry Program (IDP) - Level 3</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$17,929.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,715.00</td></tr><tr><td>Instruments, Equipment and Supplies</td><td>$1,769.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$22,413.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>International Dentistry Program (IDP) - Level 4</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$17,929.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,715.00</td></tr><tr><td>Instruments, Equipment and Supplies</td><td>$370.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$21,014.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>Doctor of Nursing Practice (Leadership)</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$11,118.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$11,118.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><p>Students do not pay Student Health &amp; Counseling Services Fee, Student Health Insurance Fee, or Student Health &amp; Counseling Supplemental Fee; therefore, these services are not available to students.</p><hr><table><caption>Doctor of Nursing Practice (Post-BSN)</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Summer Student Services Fee</td><td>$80.00</td></tr><tr><td>Tuition</td><td>$4,380.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td>Professional Degree Supplemental Tuition</td><td>$5,976.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$12,682.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><table><caption>Global Health - MS</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$11,796.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$14,042.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>Genetic Counseling - 2nd year</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$10,869.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$13,115.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>Health Data Science - MS</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$8,976.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$3,277.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$12,253.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life. .</p><hr><table><caption>Health Data Science - Certificate</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$8,976.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$3,277.00</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td>$12,253.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><hr><table><caption>Advanced Training in Clinical Research (Certificate)</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$8,370.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><p>Students do not pay Student Health &amp; Counseling Services Fee, Student Health Insurance Fee, or Student Health &amp; Counseling Supplemental Fee; therefore, these services are not available to students.</p><hr><table><caption>Clinical and Epidemiological Research - MS</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$8,370.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><p>Students do not pay Student Health &amp; Counseling Services Fee, Student Health Insurance Fee, or Student Health &amp; Counseling Supplemental Fee; therefore, these services are not available to students.</p><hr><table><caption>Healthcare Administration and Interprofessional Leadership</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Program Fee**</td><td>$15,220.00</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The cost per course for this program is $5,074.</p><p>**The program fee includes instruction, library, Graduate Division, and services provided by the following SAA units:&nbsp; Office of the Registrar, Student Financial Services, Educational Technology Services, Student Information Systems, Institutional Research, International Students &amp; Scholars Office, SAA Vice Provost's Office, Office of Career &amp; Professional Development, Learning Resource Services, Student Disability Services, and Student Life.</p><p>Students do not pay Student Health &amp; Counseling Services Fee, Student Health Insurance Fee, or Student Health &amp; Counseling Supplemental Fee; therefore, these services are not available to students.</p><hr><table><caption>Additional Summer Fees for: Off-campus students who are returning from UC Berkeley; new students; readmitted students; students who used Filing Fee status for spring 2025; and students who are no longer in Student Employee status:</caption><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Fee Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Student Health Insurance Premium</td><td>$2,246.00</td></tr><tr><td>Summer Health Insurance - Medicine, new or returning</td><td>$1,132.00</td></tr><tr><td>Disability Insurance - for new and readmitted medicine students, MSTP students (returning to Medicine program), Joint Medicine Program, MD/MPH students registering at UCSF</td><td>$10.00</td></tr><tr><td>Disability Insurance - for readmitted dentistry students</td><td>$18.00</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2>Special Rules for Summer Fees</h2><ul><li>Nonresident supplemental tuition is not charged in summer session.</li><li>Summer session fees are set annually and may differ from the regular quarter fees.</li><li>Continuing students who have been enrolled continuously in the previous academic year will be covered for student health and the Campus Community Centers Facility fee.</li><li>Readmitted students, Joint Program (UCSF-UCB) students, and students who used Filing Fee status in spring 2025 will be charged additional fees for student health service and insurance if they register for summer session, but they will not be charged the Campus Community Centers Facility fee. To use the fitness and recreation centers in summer, these students should pay a fee to the centers directly.</li><li>New and Readmitted students in Medicine, MSTP students returning to Medicine program, MDMPH, &amp; Joint Medicine Program (UCSF-UCB) registering at UCSF are charged prorated disability insurance.</li></ul></div> </div> </article> </div> </div>\n<div> <div> <div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <aside> <div> <nav role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"block-sb-nine-mainmenu-menu\"> <h2><span>Registration</span></h2> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/registration/summer-2026-registration\">Summer 2026 Registration</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/spring-2026-registration\">Spring 2026 Registration</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/how-register\">How To Register</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees\">Fees</a> <ul> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/dentistry2025\">School of Dentistry</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/school-of-medicine-2025-26\">School of Medicine</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/nursing2025\">School of Nursing</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/pharmacy2025\">School of Pharmacy</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/globalhealth2025\">Global Health Sciences</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/graddiv2025\">Graduate Division</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/summer2025\" aria-current=\"page\">Summer Session</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/transitpass\">Student Transit Pass</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/ucgpc\">UCGPC Systemwide Fee</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/fees/archived\">Archived Fees</a> </li> </ul> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/paying-fees\">Paying Fees</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/study-list-filing\">Study List Filing</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/deadlineshome\">Deadlines</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/change-study-list\">Changes To Study List</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/residency\">California Residency</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/withdrawal\">Withdrawal &amp; Leave of Absence</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/refunds\">Refunds</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/readmission\">Readmission After Absence</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/id-cards\">ID Cards</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/intercampus-exchange\">Intercampus Exchange</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/sf-consortium\">SF Consortium</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/stanford-exchange\">Stanford Exchange</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/reduced-fee-enrollment\">Reduced Fee Enrollment</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/part-time-enrollment\">Part-time Enrollment</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"/registration/summer-session-info\">Summer Session Information</a> </li> </ul> </nav> </div> </aside> <aside> <div> <div> <div> <h2>Quick Links</h2> <div> <div><p><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/studentportal/\" target=\"_blank\">Student Portal Login</a><br><a href=\"/academic-calendar\">Academic Calendar</a><br><a href=\"http://catalog.ucsf.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">General Catalog</a><br><a href=\"https://saa.ucsf.edu/courseschedule/\" target=\"_blank\">Schedule of Classes</a><br><a href=\"/forms\">Forms</a><br><a href=\"/registration/deadlineshome\">Deadlines</a><br><a href=\"/registration/fees\">Fees</a><br><a href=\"/registration/residency\" title=\"California Residency\">California Residency</a></p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </aside> </div> </div> </div> </main>",
